    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a burrito\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for street-cart shawarma out of your own spice rack. The yogurt does the marinade and the sauce, and the pickles cost almost nothing.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "Shawarma flavor lives in the spice rack, and it is cheapest to buy cumin, coriander, paprika and turmeric in bags from an international grocer rather than branded jars.",
                       "Greek yogurt is both the marinade and the sauce here, so buy the big tub. It tenderizes the chicken and then cools it down.",
                       "A jar of pickles is the cheap secret that makes this taste like a real shawarma. Buy the spears and slice them thin.",
                       "Chicken breast in the family pack is the best value. Marinate what you need and freeze the rest."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Whisk about half the Greek yogurt with the ground cumin, coriander, smoked paprika, turmeric, salt, black pepper and half the minced garlic. Coat the chicken breast and let it marinate at least 30 minutes.",
                    "Whisk the rest of the Greek yogurt with the remaining garlic, the lemon juice and the olive oil to make the garlic sauce.",
                    "Sear the marinated chicken in a hot pan until charred at the edges and cooked through, then slice it thin.",
                    "Lay sliced chicken down each tortilla with a share of sliced onion, halved cherry tomatoes and thin-sliced pickles, then spoon on the garlic yogurt sauce.",
                    "Weigh the chicken, onion and tomato together, subtract the empty bowl, and divide by 14 so each burrito gets the same fill.",
                    "Fold in the sides, roll tight, wrap each one, and portion into 14 containers."
                ],
    "portion_html":  "Weigh the sliced chicken and vegetables, subtract the empty bowl, and divide by 14, then sauce and roll each tortilla to match. Each burrito carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e. Keep the garlic sauce in a side cup if you are freezing these and add it fresh after reheating.",
